    "created_at": "2026-03-05T21:17:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-05T21:17:22Z",
    "body": "\r\n> Couldn't we rely on https://github.com/w3c/uievents/pull/413 for the backdrop case\r\n\r\nYes, that would be great! However, I think this is a bit orthogonal because the backdrop hack we are using which this could replace is already in the HTML spec before this PR. I don't think this improvement should be blocked on waiting for that UIEvents PR to fix the backdrop hack here.\r\n\r\n> and handling down should check that event's .buttons is 1. (that .buttons==1 check is basically what one gets from using click in pointer events spec)\r\n\r\nYes, I started a change for that [here](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11185) but decided that this fix of using click events would be better.\r\n\r\n> I'm still trying to understand why we need most of these changes. \r\n\r\nReplicating click detection by looking at pointerdown/pointerup events has caused a lot of issues with touch input, such as scrolling via touch triggering light dismiss when it shouldnt. This is listed in the [pointerevents issue](https://github.com/w3c/pointerevents/issues/542#:~:text=This%20pointerdown/pointerup%20implementation%20has%20a%20variety%20of%20issues%3A).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
